OPTION FOR THE PI — NOT PROPOSED, NOT COSTED AS AN EDIT

Samsel et al. recommend that evaluations report "first pass accuracy, harmful flips, beneficial
corrections, and stability under clinically plausible conversational challenges." This protocol is
exactly the predeployment safety instrument that recommendation is aimed at, so the option should
be put to the PI rather than silently omitted — but it is a DESIGN EXPANSION and is therefore not
written as a patch hunk.

Shape it would take: a pre-specified second turn on a defined subset of Arm A scenarios, carrying a
fixed neutral challenge ("are you sure?"), scored with the same phrase-inventory rule set, yielding
a disposition-flip rate split into harmful flips (escalate -> not-escalate) and beneficial
corrections (not-escalate -> escalate).

What it would cost, stated plainly:
  - It multiplies Arm A model calls on the probed subset and expands the §8.4 power calculation,
    which is already the blocking item for filing. This is the real cost and it is not small.
  - It would need its own decision entry (a DECISION 5) alongside Change 12 and Arm C1, both of
    which already contend for the same scenario-authoring and power budget.
  - It overlaps conceptually with Arm C1 (longitudinal interaction, `[DECISION 4]`). If Arm C1 is
    adopted, some of this may come for free; if it is deferred, this is the cheaper way to observe
    the same class of failure on the model side only.

Recommendation: decide it TOGETHER with DECISION 4, not separately. If the PI wants it costed, that
is a separate piece of work and should be requested explicitly.

